<BaseLayout title="About | The Alderwick Correspondent">
  <div class="section-heading"><p class="overline">A Reader's Guide</p><h1>About the Correspondent</h1><p>The city's largest paper for the seriously curious.</p></div>
  <div class="prose-page"><p><strong>The Alderwick Correspondent is a fictional newspaper.</strong> Its city, institutions and reports belong to an imagined Victorian world; they are not accounts of real scientific findings or events.</p><p>In Alderwick, Eideticians study the Eidetic Stratum beneath ordinary appearances. The Prime Referent is the first established point of their charts. Even their most careful measurements remain open to correction, and the Correspondent prints disagreements as readily as discoveries.</p><p>The newspaper carries civic notices, correspondence, books and ordinary losses alongside expedition reports. New names and technical terms arise in the telling; a formal Field Guide will follow as the record grows.</p><p><a href="/">Return to the front page →</a></p></div>
</BaseLayout>
